5268"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":250741,"output_tokens":4037,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State how the reaper and XFS quota coexist (reaper stands down vs. stays as belt-and-suspenders when the kernel is accounting) and define var_tmp_cleanup_active so it reads alive under whichever regime var_tmp_hard_quota_in_effect reports live — so the heartbeat cannot false-page when the stronger quota ceiling is what is actually enforcing.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Mechanism 1 calls XFS pquota 'the real ceiling' and mechanism 3 calls the reaper 'what actually holds the budget today', but the plan never says whether the reaper timer is disabled, left running, or made a no-op once the quota is accounting.","AC: 'publishes an enforcement-alive heartbeat on every probe tick (var_tmp_cleanup_active, 1/0 ...) so a silently-dead timer or a stale drop-in is detectable' — but if enforcement is by quota and the reaper timer is intentionally off, a timer-only heartbeat reads 0 and the treat_missing_data=breaching saturation-adjacent alarm would page on a healthy box.","The companion var_tmp_hard_quota_in_effect metric names the regime but the plan does not tie the cleanup_active semantics to it."],"finding":"The plan does not specify how the bounded reaper and the XFS project quota coexist when the quota is the live enforcer, nor what the var_tmp_cleanup_active heartbeat reports in that regime — leaving a possible false-page (heartbeat reads dead while enforcement is actually healthy via quota) or a silent double-enforcement.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fed62e8c9485f7a5e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"The design ambiguity, resolved (mechanisms 1 & 3); Acceptance Criteria — the var_tmp_cleanup_active heartbeat line","norm_id":"neabad45c5403f9d3","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator enables rootflags=pquota and reboots; the installer now enforces via quota; if the reaper timer is disabled, cleanup_active goes 0 and its alarm pages despite enforcement being live and stronger.","Both quota and reaper are left active and the two evict against each other or the heartbeat conflates 'timer alive' with 'enforcement alive'."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that var_tmp_cleanup_active is the OR of 'reaper timer/drop-in healthy' and 'hard_quota_in_effect==1', and say explicitly whether the reaper continues to run (harmlessly) under a live quota or is disabled; wire the cleanup-not-active alarm to that composite so the quota regime does not read as a dead cleanup path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Correct the observability.sh precedent citation: §2g does not exist — point to the actual per-generator section labels present (e.g. §2f Docker accumulator and the unlabeled /var/gerrit generator near line 675), or add the §2g label if intended.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'infra/scripts/observability.sh §2f/§2g are the per-generator precedents; pct_of_cap and the bounded wrapper are reused'","search_files for '§2g' in observability.sh returned (no matches)","Existing labeled sections found: §2b (line 230), §2d, §2e, §2f (line 603); the /var/gerrit generator at line 675 reads '§2 above answers \"how full is /var/gerrit\"' with no §2g label","pct_of_cap (line 487) and bounded (line 382) do exist and are correctly citable"],"finding":"The Grounding section cites 'observability.sh §2f/§2g are the per-generator precedents', but observability.sh contains no §2g section label — only §2b through §2f exist; the /var/gerrit generator precedent is at line 675 under an unlabeled '§2'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f97aff1d8a3916a86","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Grounding section — first bullet ('observability.sh §2f/§2g ...')","norm_id":"nb14e22ecf9c3cb70","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer follows the citation to locate the §2g precedent and cannot find it, wasting time or reusing the wrong section as a template."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change 'observability.sh §2f/§2g are the per-generator precedents' to reference the sections that exist (§2f for the Docker accumulator and the /var/gerrit generator block around line 675), or introduce a §2g label on that block first.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"na","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the exact XFS-quota CLI surface the installer and the regime heartbeat depend on — the limit-set path (`xfs_quota -x -c 'limit ...'` and any `/etc/projects`/`/etc/projid` project setup) and the accounting-state probe (`xfs_quota -x -c 'state'` or the `/proc/mounts` prjquota field) — and mark each MATCH/UNVERIFIED against the deployment host's xfsprogs.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5975,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'The installer applies the limit only when the kernel is already accounting, and otherwise prints the exact steps.'","Plan AC: 'var_tmp_hard_quota_in_effect ... says which regime is live'","ABSENCE: no `xfs_quota`, `projid`, or `/etc/projects` reference anywhere in the plan or repo (search_files: no matches) — the quota-set and accounting-probe commands are unnamed","Evidence class: Partially-verified — the XFS project-quota integration exists and its reboot precondition is correctly stated, but the specific command/flag surface (limit-set and state-read) is unconfirmed"],"finding":"The plan asserts the installer 'applies the [XFS project-quota] limit only when the kernel is already accounting' and publishes a `var_tmp_hard_quota_in_effect` regime heartbeat, but never names the concrete CLI surface it will invoke — neither the quota-application command (e.g. `xfs_quota -x -c 'limit ...'` plus `/etc/projects`/`/etc/projid` project setup) nor the accounting-state probe (e.g. `xfs_quota -x -c 'state'` or the `/proc/mounts` prjquota flag). The `bhard`/`pquota` mechanism itself is standard XFS and the reboot gap is correctly named and routed around, so this is not a feasibility blocker; but the specific subcommand/flag surface the installer and the regime heartbeat depend on is asserted-but-unverified, which is the flag-level mismatch T3 exists to catch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4c7cb978d78705e6","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"The design ambiguity, resolved (mechanism 1); AC line 'A second heartbeat (var_tmp_hard_quota_in_effect) says which regime is live'","norm_id":"n29a9f46ac55da2f2","priority":0.3025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Installer ships with a quota-set command whose flags differ from the running xfsprogs (e.g. missing `-p`/project-id form), silently failing to set `bhard` while reporting success","The `var_tmp_hard_quota_in_effect` probe infers the accounting regime from a command or /proc field that does not expose it on AL2023's kernel, so the heartbeat reads a plausible-but-wrong regime"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.55,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the rollback path: how to disable the reaper timer and remove the tmpfiles drop-in / alarms quickly (e.g. `systemctl disable --now`, drop-in removal), and note it in the runbook.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.818,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan installs 'reaper units', 'tmpfiles drop-in', and 'dedicated alarms' via compose-up.sh wiring.","No section states how to disable or roll back the reaper timer / drop-in / alarms after deploy.","T12(b): 'an explicit, cheap, tested way to undo the change quickly without data cleanup.'"],"finding":"The plan installs an actively-deleting reaper timer, a tmpfiles drop-in, and CloudWatch alarms as a runtime behavior change on a deployed host, but does not state a rollback/undo path — how to quickly disable the reaper (which deletes files) or revert the tmpfiles/alarm state if the mechanism misbehaves (e.g. reaper evicting too aggressively or a bad cap value causing thrash).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f99ea1660d26dff3b","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n033b30daffedb5fe","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify reaper concurrency: ensure a running reaper invocation is not re-entered by the next timer tick (systemd serializes a service by default) and that deletion is idempotent under retry.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.818,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'A bounded oldest-first reaper timer' running every 5 minutes deletes files.","Plan specifies a 900s grace window for fresh files but does not state whether concurrent/overlapping reaper runs are prevented (e.g. systemd timer/service overrun serialization).","T9 concurrency: 'shared/mutable state mutated atomically ... no check-then-act TOCTOU; idempotent under retry.'"],"finding":"The reaper mutates shared state (/var/tmp) by deleting files on a timer, but the plan does not address concurrency between overlapping reaper invocations (a run exceeding the interval while the next fires) or between the reaper and in-flight generators writing to a file it is about to delete — beyond the grace window for freshly-created files.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2558e93b33639c8c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"The design ambiguity, resolved (mechanism 3 — bounded oldest-first reaper)","norm_id":"n63d1e845af86c8b4","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"1fd2e4a65e5ccafe","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["38f0dc7072a53c15",5657],"description_boxes":["83b7db61ca19